Task: Fix input lock persisting across scene re-launch. Root cause: Phaser reuses scene instances on scene.start(); inputLocked is a field initializer (runs once at construction) and handleComplete() leaves it true, so the next launch rendered but ignored input. Regression tests: complete a playthrough, call create() again on the same instance, assert inputLocked=false and a tap registers (correct chime / pop tick). Fix: reset inputLocked=false in create() of WordMatchScene and WordBuilderScene. Note: AlphabetScene/PatternBuilderScene/MusicalMemoryScene share the same field pattern and likely the same latent bug - flagged to user, not changed.
